{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNaZtYVX6awHXNfbMrpA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016PHXq5ounPRcj5mQpgvZ65","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-878\\docs\\reviews\\wi-878\\003-ADJUDICATE-c94b1ed.md","content":"# WI-878 checkpoint sitting at c94b1ed\n\n## amendment\n\nSeven approved rows moved against their copies, recorded at commit b65b30462. All seven carry one change, the Done-when's: a dispute verdict's binding records the findings file its brief was composed over, and the coverage gate reads exactly that file, and no sibling, to show that a cited DISMISS or SUCCESSOR ruled the excluded finding. A binding without the record, which every dispute bound before this change is, refuses the citation by name.\n\nChecks I ran:\n- The arms map's eight test nodes pass (12 cases with their parameters).\n- `trace.py --strict` exits 0, with no advisory on these rows.\n- Every evidence node of TC-069, TC-327 and TC-334 resolves, and each new node is cited by the TC whose clause it holds.\n- A token check finds no code name added to any amended cell. The only new marks are HEAD and TOML.\n\nAll seven rows changed MEANING, and I would bless all seven. The rung is released, so the later act turn re-attests each.\n\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-069 Detail -> before: an F# exclusion citing a dispute verdict resolves when the cited accepted DISMISS or SUCCESSOR rules it and the findings file beside that verdict records the finding with that F#'s text -> after: the findings file is the one the verdict's binding records, read at the same reading as the verdict and binding. A binding with no record refuses by name. So does a recorded file that cannot be read, is outside the declared shape, holds no such id or holds another text. No other findings file is read -> not the same: the source of the correspondence moves from \"a file beside the verdict\" to \"the file the binding records\", and a pre-change binding that used to resolve now refuses. Ready to bless. It is the Done-when's rule word for word, fail-closed in every listed shape, and it closes the two-rounds-reusing-ids collision. It adds no name.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-069 Expected, Method, Tier -> before: the plan-coverage cases with the dispute-ruling arms, at Smoke -> after: the same, plus:\n  - two rounds reusing ids, each resolving its own finding;\n  - round 1's verdict cited for round 2's same-id finding, which refuses;\n  - a binding without the record refusing even with a matching sibling file;\n  - missing, directory, non-TOML and no-such-id recorded files refusing;\n  - the pass-record route at HEAD refusing an unrecorded dismissal;\n  - the entry-point dispute resolving only its own round's finding;\n  - the tier moved to Full.\n\n  -> not the same: new arms enter the verified set, and the run moves out of the smoke tier. Ready to bless. Each Expected clause matches an LLR-069 sentence and a named, existing case. Full is honest, because one evidence node (`test_at_the_cap_a_dismissal_bound_without_its_findings_file_is_refused`) lives in a slow module.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-327 Expected, Method -> before: the done-when and combined-sitting binding arms -> after: the same, plus a dispute brief's findings-file record bound at reservation and kept through the accepted or failed outcome rewrite, with a brief naming none binding none -> not the same: a new arm. Ready to bless. It matches LLR-310's new sentences, and `test_a_dispute_binding_records_its_findings_file_through_the_outcome` holds all three outcomes.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-310 Detail -> before: the binding records pending, the requested kinds and the outcome, through one writer and one outcome recorder -> after: the same, plus a dispute binding records its composed brief's findings file, written by the one writer in the same call as the requested ids on either route, carried unchanged by the outcome rewrite as the identity cell is; a brief naming none binds none, read as absent -> not the same: a new binding cell and its lifecycle. Ready to bless. It keeps the one-writer rule, and it states the absent case that LLR-069 refuses on, so the producer and the consumer agree.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-314 Detail -> before: the dispute grammar's findings-file reader, request line and ruling parser -> after: the same, plus the composed brief's findings-file line, whose first occurrence supplies the path, with none or an empty one supplying none -> not the same: a new grammar line. Ready to bless. It is closed (first line wins, and an empty line supplies nothing), and TC-334's new clause and case hold it.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-315 Detail -> before: `dispute_values` fills the request with the requested ids -> after: the request also carries, after the ids, the findings-file line naming the one reference the assembler read -> not the same: the composed brief carries a new line. Ready to bless. It ties the record to the file actually read, which is the Trust section's producer rule (the binding records the path `dispute_values` read), and it adds no name: the function was named in the approved cell already.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-334 Expected, Method -> before: the dispute brief, grammar, verdict and entry-point arms -> after: the same, plus the composed brief naming its findings file on a line the grammar reads back -> not the same: a new arm. Ready to bless. `test_the_dispute_brief_names_the_findings_file_it_was_composed_over` holds it, and it matches LLR-314 and LLR-315.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=7\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":943,"cache_read_input_tokens":562595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":943},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","spee